  Split out of the combined Enrolments and Requests screen. The two lists had shared one route and
  one page, switched by in-page tab buttons, which meant neither could be linked to, bookmarked or
  reloaded on its own and the browser's back button could not return to the one the reader was on.
  They are separate screens now, reached from the shared Courses tab strip that every screen in the
  group renders in the same place.

  Core owns this markup. Themes style it through the ordinary platform table, form and button
  classes.

  Comments here are plain prose only: no angle brackets, no comment delimiters, no template tokens
  and no code. Each of those is read as markup rather than as text.

